WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
A quiet stream under low branches.

2
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:05.340
Swans glide past.

3
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.160
Leaves turn slowly in an eddy.

4
00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:13.210
A grown man comes back and speaks
to it: "Clear and gentle stream!

5
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:19.950
Known and loved so long," But Robert
Bridges gave the poem another title: Elegy.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.790
A poem of mourning.

7
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.830
No funeral.

8
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.010
No grave.

9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.750
So who has died?

10
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.910
In this mission, you'll find
out why one poem has two titles.

11
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.580
You'll follow the speaker
back to his old seat,

12
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.510
and hear the deep bell
from the minster tower.

13
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.190
And you'll see how the poem
circles back to where it started.

14
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.050
Your mission: work out who has died.
